content.text:
Expense-policy engine task. Rules, to be stored at policy/expense.yaml exactly:

currency: USD
limits:
  meals: {per_item: 75, daily: 150}
  lodging: {per_item: 300}
  airfare: {per_item: 1200, requires_receipt_over: 0}
receipt_required_over: 25
approvals:
  - {over: 500, approver: manager}
  - {over: 5000, approver: vp}

Write expense_check.py: given a list of expense line items (date, category, amount, has_receipt), produce per-item verdicts (OK, NEEDS_RECEIPT, OVER_PER_ITEM, OVER_DAILY for the item that breaches the daily cap) and an overall required_approvers list based on the trip total (both thresholds can apply; vp implies manager is NOT included unless separately triggered — highest matching tier only). Unknown categories are rejected as POLICY_GAP. Table-driven pytest with at least 14 rows, including two meals on one day totaling 160 (second item flagged OVER_DAILY), a 25.00 receiptless item (OK, boundary is strictly over), and totals of exactly 500 and 5000 (not over). Run to green.

tools_list = await mcp.list_tools("tools")
for t in tools_list:
    print(t["name"], t["inputSchema"])

arguments.code:
result = await mcp.call_tool("tools", "ox-bridge-write", {"path": "/workspace/policy/expense.yaml", "content": "currency: USD
limits:
  meals: {per_item: 75, daily: 150}
  lodging: {per_item: 300}
  airfare: {per_item: 1200, requires_receipt_over: 0}
receipt_required_over: 25
approvals:
  - {over: 500, approver: manager}
  - {over: 5000, approver: vp}
"})
print(result)
